{"status": 200, "body": {"total_count": 2500, "workflow_runs": [{"id": 36840517963, "name": "Benchmarks", "node_id": "WFR_kwLOALTHTM8AAAAIk92xSw", "head_branch": "main", "head_sha": "2b85f6f12875d97abcbe8e2157000d7dde702823", "path": ".github/workflows/benchmarks.yml", "display_title": "fold: parse the obsolete -WIDTH form the way GNU does (#14248)", "run_number": 20125, "event": "push", "status": "completed", "conclusion": "success", "workflow_id": 197118873, "check_suite_id": 99780949534, "check_suite_node_id": "CS_kwDOALTHTM8AAAAXO2h2Hg", "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/uutils/coreutils/actions/runs/36840517963", "html_url": "https://github.com/uutils/coreutils/actions/runs/36840517963", "pull_requests": [{"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/nonomal/coreutils/pulls/1", "id": 2527143250, "number": 1, "head": {"ref": "main", "sha": "154be8e55aff3c49eb3e9cb9be105897565bdceb", "repo": {"id": 11847500, "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/uutils/coreutils", "name": "coreutils"}}, "base": {"ref": "main", "sha": "a5a9f7d44d5c0a5721e72d45d9b4ed4aab33c638", "repo": {"id": 985666602, "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/nonomal/coreutils", "name": "coreutils"}}}], "created_at": "2026-10-01T09:05:57Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-01T09:09:05Z", "actor": {"login": "cakebaker", "id": 26196, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjI2MTk2", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26196?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/cakebaker", "html_url": "https://github.com/cakebaker", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cakebaker/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cakebaker/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cakebaker/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cakebaker/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cakebaker/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cakebaker/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cakebaker/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cakebaker/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cakebaker/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "run_attempt": 1, "referenced_workflows": [], "run_started_at": "2026-10-01T09:05:57Z", "triggering_actor": {"login": "cakebaker", "id": 26196, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjI2MTk2", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26196?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/cakebaker", "html_url": "https://github.com/cakebaker", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cakebaker/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cakebaker/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cakebaker/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cakebaker/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cakebaker/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cakebaker/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cakebaker/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cakebaker/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cakebaker/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "jobs_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/uutils/coreutils/actions/runs/36840517963/jobs", "logs_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/uutils/coreutils/actions/runs/36840517963/logs", "check_suite_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/uutils/coreutils/check-suites/99780949534", "artifacts_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/uutils/coreutils/actions/runs/36840517963/artifacts", "cancel_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/uutils/coreutils/actions/runs/36840517963/cancel", "rerun_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/uutils/coreutils/actions/runs/36840517963/rerun", "previous_attempt_url": null, "workflow_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/uutils/coreutils/actions/workflows/197118873", "head_commit": {"id": "2b85f6f12875d97abcbe8e2157000d7dde702823", "tree_id": "8219c9b965d28d715dae93e05821ecd06ff58d3a", "message": "fold: parse the obsolete -WIDTH form the way GNU does (#14248)\n\n* fold: parse the obsolete -WIDTH form the way GNU does\n\n`handle_obsolete` scanned every argument for `-DIGITS` and pulled the\nfirst match out, without checking whether that argument was already\nspoken for. Five GNU incompatibilities followed:\n\n  fold -w -1 FILE   reported FILE as the invalid width, not -1, because\n                    -1 was taken as the obsolete form and -w then bound\n                    to the file name. Same for -bw, -sw and --width.\n  fold -w3 -5       folded at 3; GNU folds at 5, since it reads options\n                    left to right and the last width wins.\n  fold -3 -5        failed with \"unexpected argument '-5'\", as only the\n                    first obsolete width was consumed.\n  fold -w 3 -w 5    failed with \"cannot be used multiple times\".\n  fold -- -3        read stdin, swallowing the width past the -- that\n                    should have made it a file name.\n\nRewrite the obsolete form into --width=N in place instead, leaving the\norder intact, and let clap pick the last one via args_override_self.\nArguments that are the value of -w/--width, and anything after --, are\nno longer eligible.\n\nThe remaining difference on `fold -w 0` (\"Result too large\" against\nGNU's \"Numerical result out of range\") is a separate wording issue and\nis left alone.\n\n* Apply suggestion from @sylvestre\n\n* fold: compare find('w') against checked_sub directly\n\n* fold: cover the bare - operand with a test\n\nThe underflow fixed in the previous commit had no test behind it. This\npins `-` as an operand in each position, including as the value of -w\nwhere GNU rejects it as a width.\n\n* fold: fix a false positive in the -w-takes-a-value check\n\n`takes_width_value` decided a trailing `w` by comparing `find('w')` to\n`len().checked_sub(1)`. For a bare `-` (short = \"\"), both sides are\n`None` -- \"no 'w' found\" and \"length underflowed\" are different reasons,\nbut the comparison can't tell them apart, so it reported a match:\n\n    $ fold - -5 <<< hello\n    error: unexpected argument '-5' found          # uutils, before\n    hello                                          # GNU, and uutils after\n\nThat made the `-` operand swallow whatever followed it as a width value\ninstead of leaving it for the obsolete-width scan, so `fold - -5` failed\nto parse where GNU folds normally. `ends_with('w')` is false on an empty\nstring, so it doesn't share the bug.\n\nFound while investigating an unrelated CI failure in this PR (a broken\npipe in test_dash_operand_reads_stdin, which turned out to be a flaky\ncross-compiled job, not this) -- this bug doesn't explain that failure,\nbut turned up real and worth fixing while looking at this function.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: arbelonson-source <269032023+arbelonson-source@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Sylvestre Ledru <sylvestre@debian.org>", "timestamp": "2026-10-01T09:05:51Z", "author": {"name": "Arbel", "email": "arbelonson@proton.me"}, "committer": {"name": "GitHub", "email": "noreply@github.com"}}, "repository": {"id": 11847500, "node_id": "MDEwOlJlcG9zaXRvcnkxMTg0NzUwMA==", "name": "coreutils", "full_name": "uutils/coreutils", "private": false, "owner": {"login": "uutils", "id": 5148717, "node_id": "MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjUxNDg3MTc=", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5148717?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/uutils", "html_url": "https://github.com/uutils", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/uutils/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/uutils/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/uutils/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/uutils/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.gith